      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T13:30:52Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, deployment and implementation-install anchors, transaction-local implementation-slot state diff, pre-exploit implementation slot and runtime hash, the verified L1ChugSplashProxy and ProxyAdmin architecture, every external and internal call to ProxyAdmin 0xba86cd28d937f1cc7c74a365368477408578364a from proxy deployment through the pre-exploit block, the commit-pinned reproduction, Verichains analysis, and reported loss. The exploit executes bridge proxy 0x40c31236b228935b0329eff066b1ad96e319595e and delegates to 0xe468b43b4ae4d750cd6a5d7edacc1a751302c99c. Of the 12 successful external ProxyAdmin calls in that interval, transaction 0x4cdfc7580172bee1a1decbe6190e0a018533259f324923c059f2833336cd0351 is the only call selecting code for this bridge; no internal ProxyAdmin calls occurred. Its state diff changes the proxy's EIP-1967 implementation slot from zero to 0xe468b43b4ae4d750cd6a5d7edacc1a751302c99c, and that value and runtime remain present immediately before the exploit. The transaction transferred exactly 2,570,000 HYPR from bridge custody."
